From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 19:15:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11110/11362] [outer-loop] Correct the observability claim: the
 eval is watchable per attempt

An hour ago this file said the within-game blind spot was untouched. Half
wrong. results/arc_e3/<game>/attempts/evidence/ gains a sealed directory per
completed induction attempt, and .evidence-staging/ holds the one in flight,
so a long single-game run reports progress every 30 to 60 minutes with no new
tooling. The r11l run has emitted two engines already, verifiable 90 minutes
before its artifact will exist.

Found by accident: a conductor checkpoint commit swept the files, which is the
only reason anyone looked. The signal was there the whole time while the check
watched the run artifact and the log.

Still true and now stated precisely: a directory appears only when an attempt
SEALS, so a hung attempt shows nothing and the blind spot inside one attempt
is untouched.

Checked against the engine-store regression memory: all 15 historical wm_*.py
engines survive, including the four scored today. Two storage shapes now
coexist and a count of one looks like deletion of the other.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
