+### 23:20Z — the running eval IS observable, and it has already emitted two engines
+
+**CORRECTION 4.** At 22:30Z this file said the within-game blind spot was untouched and was the
+real remaining observability work. That is half wrong, and the half that is wrong was found by
+accident: a conductor checkpoint commit swept files from the running eval, which is how anyone
+noticed they existed.
+
+`results/arc_e3/<game>/attempts/` gains a sealed directory per COMPLETED induction attempt under
+`evidence/`, named `arc-<UTC start>_<micros>-<hash>`, holding `engine.py`, `envelope.json`,
+`environment_receipt.json`, `transitions.jsonl`, `prompt.raw` and the policy sources. An attempt
+still running sits in `.evidence-staging/` under the same name; sealing is a move between the
+two.
+
+The r11l run (PID 3114878, started 21:23Z) as of 23:13Z:
+
+| attempt | started | sealed | engine.py |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | 21:24Z | 22:30Z, about 66 min | 4,270 B |
+| 2 | 22:30Z | 23:03Z, about 33 min | 8,374 B |
+| 3 | 23:03Z | in `.evidence-staging/` | — |
+
+**Two engines are already emitted.** The run is doing what it was authorized to do, and that was
+verifiable 90 minutes before its artifact will exist. No new instrumentation was needed; the
+signal was in the evidence tree while everyone watched the run artifact and the log.
+
+Limits, so this is not over-read. A directory appears only when an attempt SEALS, so a HUNG
+attempt still shows nothing, and the blind spot inside a single attempt is real and untouched.
+The 30-to-60-minute cadence is one run on one game, not a general rate.
+
+**Checked because a memory warns about it: nothing was destroyed.** All 15 historical
+`attempts/wm_<UTC>__<hash>.py` engines are present, including the four post-fix ones scored in
+the 22:05Z table (`wm_20260904T020536`, `T062427`, `T071247`, `T074908`). Two storage shapes now
+coexist: the flat `wm_*.py` files, and the evidence directories that arrived today with the
+producer evidence contract (exp6993, exp6994). **Count both shapes.** Counting one looks exactly
+like the other was deleted, which is the engine-store regression this project has already had
+once.
+
+**Also verified, no action needed.** The conductor's HEAD checkpoint commit (`808a9bead7`) swept
+no operator-curated document, and all five outer-loop commits from this session remain reachable
+from HEAD. Milestone .613 shows the refusal machinery working end to end rather than a fault:
+22:41 planned with 4 tasks, 22:44 activation REFUSED on 2 exclusion-manifest HARD violations and
+the roadmap quarantined, 23:01 replanned with 13 tasks, 23:05 activated. Twenty-four minutes,
+unattended, and the refusal also corrected an undersized milestone. BLOCK runs 1 to 6 per day
+historically, so today's single BLOCK is ordinary.
+
